This project uses card data from the following sources:

MTGJSON (https://mtgjson.com/)
Licensed under the MIT License
Card metadata including names, mana costs, types, oracle text, and other
game-relevant fields is sourced from MTGJSON's open data sets.

大学院废墟 — magic-cards-zhs (https://github.com/HeliumOctahelide/magic-cards-zhs)
Licensed under CC-BY-SA-4.0
Simplified-Chinese card names, Oracle text, and type lines are derived from that
project's weekly data exports by `scripts/gen-zhs-card-text.mjs`, producing the
build artifact `client/public/card-data.zhs.json`. Scryfall publishes no
Simplified-Chinese printings, so this locale cannot come from MTGJSON's
`foreignData` the way every other content language does.

The derived sidecar is a build output and is not committed; the script that
produces it, the source revision it reads, and this attribution travel with the
repository instead.

